@ 1:6  class|Diagram
  1:1-1:13 "classDiagram"
  | **`classDiagram`**
  |
  | A diagram is the header line, then statements, one per line.
@ 2:6  dir|ection LR
  2:3-2:15 "direction LR"
  | **`direction LR`** direction: left to right
@ 3:5  cl|ass A
  3:3-3:8 "class"
  | **`class`**
  |
  | `class Name`, with an optional `["label"]`, then `:::style`, `<<annotation>>` or a body of members in braces.
@ 4:7  name|space N {
  4:3-4:12 "namespace"
  | **`namespace`**
  |
  | `namespace Name { … }`: groups classes and notes.
@ 7:5  no|te for A "x"
  7:3-7:11 "note for"
  | **`note for`**
  |
  | `note for Class "text"` or `note "text"`.
@ 8:6  not|e "y"
  8:3-8:7 "note"
  | **`note`**
  |
  | `note for Class "text"` or `note "text"`.
@ 9:8  class|Def hot fill:#f00
  9:3-9:11 "classDef"
  | **`classDef`**
  |
  | `classDef name fill:#f96`: defines a style class, given with `:::name` or `cssClass`.
@ 10:6  css|Class "A" hot
  10:3-10:11 "cssClass"
  | **`cssClass`**
  |
  | `cssClass "A,B" name`: gives classes a style class.
@ 11:6  sty|le A fill:#000
  11:3-11:8 "style"
  | **`style`**
  |
  | `style Class fill:#f9f`: styles one class.
@ 12:7  call|back A "fn"
  12:3-12:11 "callback"
  | **`callback`**
  |
  | `callback Class "fn"`, `link Class "url"`, `click Class call fn()` or `click Class href "url"`, with an optional tooltip; links take an optional target.
